  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "EIP-1559 is an Ethereum Improvement Proposal implemented in the London hard fork that fundamentally reformed Ethereum's transaction fee market. It replaced the simple first-price auction mechanism with a protocol-determined base fee that automatically adjusts each block based on demand relative to a target block gas usage. The base fee is burned rather than paid to validators, creating a deflationary pressure on ether supply. Users optionally add a priority fee (tip) to incentivise timely inclusion. The mechanism improves fee predictability for users and reduces the miner extractable value (MEV) captured through fee sniping.",
